<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nguyễn Cảnh Chân</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1409</span> · Also known as Nguyen Canh Chan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nguyễn Cảnh Chân was a Vietnamese general of the Later Tran resistance against the Ming occupation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> after 1407. With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dang-tat">Dang Tat</a> he commanded the army that defeated the Ming at Bo Co in 1408. Emperor Gian Dinh had both generals killed in 1409, and Nguyen Canh Chan's son Nguyen Canh Di went on to fight for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tran-quy-khoang">Trùng Quang</a> Đế.</p></div>
